[center][size=6][b]YADS - Yet Another Digital Storage Mod[/b][/size]
[size=3][i]Network storage for Fields of Mistria. One search bar for every crate you own.[/i][/size]

[b]Beta 1.3[/b] by mykay · requires the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fieldsofmistria/mods/78]Mods of Mistria Installer[/url] 0.15.1+[/center]

[line]

[b]Back up your saves before installing any mod. It's a beta.[/b]

If you've played modded Minecraft or Terraria you already know the idea. This is my love letter to Applied Energistics 2, Refined Storage and Magic Storage: link storage units into a network and browse all of it from one terminal. Search, sort, filter, quick-stack.

[size=5][b]The units[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Storage Heart[/b] (50 Wood, 5 Copper Ingot, 1 Glass). The brain. One per network.
[*][b]Storage Block[/b] (30 Wood, 1 Copper Ingot). 30 slots each. Chain as many as you want.
[*][b]Access Panel[/b] (1 Copper Ingot, 1 Glass). The terminal. Open it to browse the network.
[*][b]Remote Access Panel[/b] (5 Ruby, 5 Sapphire, 5 Copper Ingot, 5 Iron Ingot, 1 Access Panel). Browse from anywhere.
[*][b]Network Converter[/b] (1 Copper Ingot, 1 Glass). Turns a placed chest into a crate, or a crate back into a chest.
[/list]

The first three are crafted at the Woodcrafting Station, under "Chests & Storage" and their own "Digital Storage" category. The Converter and the Remote craft under "Digital Storage" only: neither is a chest, so neither can be placed.

Place units so they touch and they link up. Connected units glow (blocks and crates tint green, yellow or red by how full they are), a disconnected one shows a sad face. Each room is its own network, so the farm and the farmhouse each need their own Heart. Don't place units on tables.

[size=5][b]Turn your chests into network storage[/b][/size]

Every convertible vanilla chest, 59 of them across every family (basic wood in all its colors, deluxe, royal, stone, coral, icebox, fridge, mist, void, obsidian, miners, dragon, the festival flower chest, even the mimic), can join your network as a crate: same exact look, same exact capacity, 30, 42 or 54 slots depending on the chest. A crate glows with the network's colors and shows the sad face when disconnected, just like a Storage Block. The mist chest floats, so its glow shows on the shadow pad beneath it instead of on the chest itself. Crates have no crafting recipe of their own, converting a chest is the only way to get one.

The Network Converter does the converting. Hold it and interact with a placed chest to wire it into the network, contents stay right where they are. Interact with a crate instead and it turns back into the plain chest it was, contents intact again. One converter spent, either direction.

[b]Upgrading is a gesture, not a rebuild.[/b] Hold a chest item and interact with any placed chest or crate: the target becomes that held chest's crate, your items carry over, and the old shell pops straight back into your backpack as an item. It costs the chest you're holding plus one converter, and it's refused with a clear message if your items wouldn't fit the new size. Craft or buy a bigger chest, hold it, tap your crate, that's the whole upgrade. The price is whatever the vanilla chest economy already charges for that tier: a deluxe crate costs you a deluxe chest, same as it always did.

[size=5][b]Wire it all together[/b][/size]

Four floor pieces carry the network between units that are too far apart to touch. Lay them in a path and everything they touch, standing on them or right beside them, joins the same network. They chain to each other too, so a carpet path can run clear across the farm.

[list]
[*][b]Magic Carpet[/b] (3 Fiber)
[*][b]Magic Tile[/b] (3 Stone)
[*][b]Bundle of Cables[/b] (2 Wood, 1 Copper Ore)
[*][b]Cloud Connector[/b] (1 Glass, 2 Fiber)
[/list]

All four are walkable, no hitbox, and you can place a chest or a crate right on top of one. They craft at Woodcrafting level 1, under "Digital Storage" only, and glow cyan once they're carrying a live network.

They're shape-aware, too. A straight run draws as one continuous line, not a row of repeated tiles: corners bend, junctions branch, and the path runs right up into the crates it feeds. The carpet only shows its fringe on open edges, the cables bundle into a real pipe with clamps, the cloud stretches into one long bank. A freshly placed piece can take a second to settle into its shape while the network catches up.

One tip: the Cloud Connector floats above the ground and has no line at ground level, so a run that mixes it with the others shows a gap where it sits. The network is still whole there, the cloud just runs its own way.

Three small things to know: building over a connector with a blueprint or farm expansion removes it without dropping the item, so re-route before you build. A connector fully covered by a chest can't be picked up until the chest moves. And connectors can't share a cell with a decorative rug, it's one rug layer per cell.

[size=5][b]Remote access[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Hand the Remote Access Panel to a Storage Heart and they're linked. Press [b]F6[/b] anywhere to browse that network, even from the bottom of the mines.
[*]Several networks? [b]Hold[/b] the key for a picker: one row per network with room, blocks and fill. Tick the checkbox on a row to make it your default, and a tap goes straight there.
[*][b]Rebind the key in game[/b]: hold the key, click Rebind key, press the one you want. Works instantly. Holding F6 always opens the picker as a backup, so a bad key can never lock you out.
[*]To unlink, take the remote back out at an Access Panel. You can't pull it out through a remote view, so you can't strand yourself from the mines.
[/list]

[size=5][b]The network view[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]The vanilla storage UI over every connected unit at once. Withdraw and deposit exactly like a chest.
[*]A real search box: full text editing, an X to clear it, Ctrl+arrows jump whole words. Auto-focus toggle so it's ready when the panel opens.
[*]14 category filters, plus a "Museum needs" lens for what the museum still wants.
[*]227 items now sort under the right filter: wood is out of Fishing, wallpapers and floorings show up under their filter again, cooked seafood is out of Fish, and more.
[*]Value badges per stack or per item. Big numbers abbreviate, like 12.3k.
[*]Five sort modes. Your pick is remembered.
[*]Quick-stack your backpack into the network with one button.
[*]Crafting stations pull from the network automatically. The units are real chests, so it just works.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]You can squeeze between crates: solid core, walkable edges.
[*]A unit that still holds items takes five pickaxe swings to break. Empty ones break in one.
[*]Blocks and crates with no heart behave as plain chests, so your items are never locked away.
[*]If a deposit doesn't fit, the rest comes straight back with a toast. Nothing is silently eaten.
[/list]

The mod never holds your items. Everything lives in the real chest inventories of the placed units, which the game's own save system writes. If the game crashes with the view open, nothing is lost.

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Extract the zip into [font=Courier New]Fields of Mistria/mods/[/font] so the file [font=Courier New]mods/yads/manifest.json[/font] exists.
[*]Run the Mods of Mistria Installer, tick [b]YADS[/b], hit Install.
[*]Play. Recipes unlock automatically, existing saves included.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Before uninstalling[/b][/size]

[b]Empty your units first.[/b] The engine drops placed objects it no longer recognizes, together with everything inside them. Backpack items are safe.

[size=5][b]Credits[/b][/size]

Applied Energistics 2, Refined Storage and Magic Storage for the genre. Built with [url=https://github.com/Garethp/Mods-of-Mistria-Installer]Mods of Mistria / MMAPI[/url], thanks to Garethp and its maintainers. And thanks to NPC Studio for shipping source readable enough to mod this deeply.

Source code: [url=https://github.com/Mihai-Tudosa/YADS]github.com/Mihai-Tudosa/YADS[/url]

Found a bug? Report it with your log file ([font=Courier New]%LOCALAPPDATA%\FieldsOfMistria\mod_data\yads\logs[/font]).

If YADS saved you an afternoon of chest-diving, you can buy me a coffee: [url=https://paypal.me/tudosamihai]paypal.me/tudosamihai[/url]. The mod is free and stays free.
